  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "My right shoulder, doctor. It is paining so much, mostly at night. When I lie on that side it wakes me up, and in the day I cannot even reach the top shelf in the kitchen.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:14",
      "end_timestamp": "01:32",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "It started just after Diwali, Mummy, so it is nearer four. But it has gotten much worse in the last month, doctor. She can't comb her hair on that side, or fasten her blouse.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:48",
      "end_timestamp": "02:04",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Four months, then, worsening. Mrs. Rao, how bad is the pain at its worst, would you call it mild, moderate or severe?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:07",
      "end_timestamp": "02:16",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Severe at night. In the day it is moderate. Is it a cancer? Everyone on my WhatsApp group says shoulder pain means the heart.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:18",
      "end_timestamp": "02:30",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I understand why you'd worry, and I'll come to that. Let me ask a few questions first. Have you had any fall or injury to the shoulder?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:31",
      "end_timestamp": "02:44",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, no fall. I have been very careful, Lakshmi holds my arm even to go to the bathroom.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:46",
      "end_timestamp": "02:54",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Any fever, or feeling hot and unwell?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:55",
      "end_timestamp": "02:59",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No fever, doctor.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:02",
      "end_timestamp": "03:04",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And any numbness or tingling down the arm into the hand?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:06",
      "end_timestamp": "03:11",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No numbness. Only the pain, and that stiffness.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:13",
      "end_timestamp": "03:17",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Sugar. I have had diabetes for fifteen years now.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:29",
      "end_timestamp": "03:33",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "They took out my gallbladder, ten years ago. In Hyderabad. Nothing since.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:45",
      "end_timestamp": "03:51",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.surgical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Let me think, there is the sugar tablet, metformin, 500 mg, twice a day after food. Then the paracetamol, 500 mg, I take it at night for the shoulder, but it hardly helps. And, Lakshmi, what was the third? The vitamin.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:01",
      "end_timestamp": "04:19",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "medications[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "speaker_role": "caregiver",
      "transcript_text": "The vitamin D, madam, one sachet on Sundays.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:20",
      "end_timestamp": "04:24",
      "supports": [
        "medications[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Let me check your blood pressure and pulse first. Blood pressure is 136 over 84, and pulse is 74.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:35",
      "end_timestamp": "04:44",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It does. Right, you can put the cardigan back on. What I found is that the right shoulder is very stiff, and you can only lift it up to about shoulder height, whether I move it or you do. The other shoulder moves freely.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:45",
      "end_timestamp": "06:09",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "This looks most likely like a frozen shoulder. It's more common in people with diabetes, and it commonly hurts most at night. It isn't cancer, and it isn't your heart.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:22",
      "end_timestamp": "06:39",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'm going to refer you to a physiotherapist who will teach you gentle stretches, which are the mainstay of treatment. In the meantime, a warm towel on the shoulder before bed, and sleep with a pillow tucked under that arm.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:19",
      "end_timestamp": "07:40",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]",
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks to see how the stiffness is moving.",
      "start_timestamp": "08:18",
      "end_timestamp": "08:26",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]",
        "follow_up[0]"
      ]
    }
